Author: Daniel Dragomir <daniel.dragomir@windriver.com>
Date:   Thu Jun 20 14:34:22 2024 +0300

    axxia-image: Fix dynamic interpreter for kernel-devsrc binaries
    
    At the end of the rootfs creation, we prepare kernel sources included
    in rootfs (make clean olddefconfig scripts modules_prepare tools/objtool)
    for compiling external modules on the board. We use the same KERNEL_CC
    compiler (x86_64-intelaxxia-linux-gcc) from the build sysroot as when
    compiling kernel during the yocto build. Because of this, the binaries
    created are dynamically linked and the interpreter is the one
    from the build sysroot:
    /buildarea/.../tmp/sysroots-uninative/x86_64-linux/lib/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2
    
    Those binaries can't be used after booting the rootfs because of the wrong
    interpreter (No such file or directory). To fix this, can use patchelf to
    change the interpreter to /lib/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 which is obtined by
    ${@get_linuxloader(d)} function.
    
    fixdep: ELF 64-bit LSB shared object, x86-64, version 1 (SYSV), dynamically linked,
            interpreter /lib/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2,
            BuildID[sha1]=e7091dc2a636918a143d93bfeb033a917b6dfe52,
            for GNU/Linux 3.2.0, not stripped
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <daniel.dragomir@windriver.com>

