commit 7528b7feb285abaf06cde0f3c9cc23321e5d62f4
Author: Daniel Dragomir <daniel.dragomir@windriver.com>
Date:   Tue Aug 1 16:04:56 2023 +0300

    Enabling Multiple Configuration Build
    
    Setup multi configuration build that can build multiple
    configurations defined in conf/multiconfig:
       ├── grr.conf
       ├── qsp.conf
       └── snr.conf
    
    This MC build can be enabled in local.conf with BBMULTICONFIG var:
        BBMULTICONFIG = "snr grr qsp"
    
    For each configuration, a specific TMPDIR will be created in BUILDDIR.
    If you need to set a different location for TMPDIR, use the TMPDIR_MULTICONFIG
    variable to set the path for all configurations.
    
    To compile the multiple configuration build, the following sintax should be used:
        bitbake [mc:multiconfigname:]target [[[mc:multiconfigname:]target] ... ]
        e.g. bitbake mc::axxia-image-dev  # compile axxia-image-dev for all configuration
             bitbake mc:snr:axxia-image-min   # compile axxia-image-run for Snow Ridge
             bitbake mc:grr:virtual/kernel  # compile the kernel for Grand Ridge
             bitbake mc:qsp:axxia-image-qsp  # compile QSP image for Simulation
    
    Be aware that the default configuration (local.conf) can be used as before.
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <daniel.dragomir@windriver.com>

