commit e199602fb903408b433ca6ede3a7305d9262472a
Author: Daniel Dragomir <daniel.dragomir@windriver.com>
Date:   Fri Jun 30 03:27:58 2023 +0300

    wic: Fix AXXIA customized source plugin
    
    A customized axxia-bootimg-efi.py wic source plugin was created
    to install alternative kernels in /boot partition and to create
    an entry for each kernel in the boot menu.
    
    But all the NEW bitbake variable used in this source plugin need
    to be specified in WICVARS variable in order to be accesible when
    wic tool creates the image. If not in WICVARS, get_bitbake_var
    function will return None and no alternative kernels will be
    installed /boot partition and the boot menu will be broken.
    
    This requirement is not necessary when the image is created
    standalone with wic command-line tool and not during the yocto
    build. In this case, variables are accesible even if are not
    included in WICVARS var. This is the reason this bug was not
    discovered sooner (the plugin was tested only with wic tool).
    
    Another fix in axxia-bootimg-efi.py wic source plugin is the check
    for any alternative kernel available in the IMAGE_INSTALL variable
    for the compiled image. This cover the case when ALTERNATIVE_KERNELS
    is defined in the distro file for the entire build, but the image
    does not include them (axxia-image-min or axxia-image-run).
    
    Without this check, the wic tool will try to install alternative
    kernels in /boot image but those kernels are not compiled because
    are not included in the min or run image as dependency.
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <daniel.dragomir@windriver.com>

