    images: Add custom images for EFI Stub test scenario
    
    Add for each Axxia image a custom one to be used in EFI
    Stub test scenario. The .wic image contains 5 /boot
    partitions (60M each with 20M free) and one for root:
    Num     Start        End          Size      Fstype
     1       1048576     63861759     62813184  fat16
     2      63963136    126776319     62813184  fat16
     3     126877696    189690879     62813184  fat16
     4     189792256    252605439     62813184  fat16
     5     252706816    315519999     62813184  fat16
     6     315621376    551344127    235722752  ext4
    
    Each boot partition contains the kernel binary (bzImage)
    with EFI STUB support, an initd image (set with
    INITRD_IMAGE_LIVE variable) and the bootloader (set with
    EFI_PROVIDER variable):
    
    root@vcn-259-nic$ ls -R /run/media/msdos1-sda1
    /run/media/msdos1-sda1:
    EFI  bzImage  initramfs.cpio.gz
    /run/media/msdos1-sda1/EFI/BOOT:
    bootx64.efi  grub.cfg
    
    All 5 /boot partitions use the same root partition which
    is identified with static UUID (set with ROOT_DISK_UUID
    variable) and choosen on bootloader options:
    root=PARTUUID=${ROOT_DISK_UUID}
    
    To boot each /boot partition it can be selected from
    the EFI shell by calling the bootx64.efi image:
    Shell> fs3:\EFI\BOOT\bootx64.efi
    
    The initrd images is also set from the bootloader options:
    initrd /initramfs.cpio.gz
    
    A0366 - GRR -- Create Disk Image for VAB Testing
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <daniel.dragomir@windriver.com>

