commit e8bc90c51e03dbf4b4ba07b0a1f30e32b6823887
Author: Daniel Dragomir <daniel.dragomir@windriver.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 8 01:15:52 2022 +0300

    linux: Alternative kernels should not provide virtual/kernel
    
    Starting with commit f748564653 ("kernel: provide virtual/kernel
    for all kernels") from poky, all kernels provide kernel virtual
    target even if KERNEL_PACKAGE_NAME is not 'kernel', but other
    alternative name. This was done to be sure each kernel should
    be used as preferred provider for virtual/kernel.
    
    The side efect is that we can't build multiple kernels in one build:
    If you set PREFERRED_PROVIDER for a virtual/* item, then any recipe
    that PROVIDES that item that is not selected by PREFERRED_PROVIDER
    is prevented from building, which is usually desirable since this
    mechanism is designed to select between mutually exclusive
    alternative providers.
    
    So, alternative kernels provides virtual/kernel alongside the main
    kernel and will exclude each other:
    ERROR: Nothing RPROVIDES 'altkernel-linux-intel-debug'
    linux-intel-debug RPROVIDES altkernel-linux-intel-debug but was skipped:
    PREFERRED_PROVIDER_virtual/kernel set to linux-intel, not linux-intel-debug
    
    To fix this, ensure only the main kernel (KERNEL_PACKAGE_NAME=kernel)
    provides virtual/kernel.
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <daniel.dragomir@windriver.com>

