Author: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>
Date:   Mon Feb 28 13:18:34 2022 +0200

    perf: Update perf pmu-events sorting tool for newer kernels
    
    When trying to build newer kernels (>5.16), perf fails because
    the pmu-events sorting tool (sort-pmuevents-new.py) from hardknott
    branch does not allow for additional type qualifiers and storage
    class: AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'group'
    This was fixed upstream in the following commit:
    
    commit 44a3909bf61a29d279a5a0a23d62cb9b0fdd3b52
    Author: Max Krummenacher <max.oss.09@gmail.com>
    Date:   Mon Nov 22 17:34:59 2021 +0100
    perf: sort-pmuevents: allow for additional type qualifiers and storage class
       With kernel 5.16 some structs in pmu-events do get a const qualifier, some
       a static const storage class and qualifier.
       The current sort-pmuevents cannot cope with that and drops all struct
       arrays with such additional elements. This then leads to compiler errors.
       Allow '^struct', '^const struct', '^static struct', '^static const struct'.
    
    Overwrite sort-pmuevents.py script with the updated one. It works
    fine with older versions of kernel too.

