Author: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 11 02:19:30 2021 +0200

    python3: autoreconf in-tree libffi for 3.6 version
    
    The _ctypes python3 modules is compiled from python3 sources
    and it requires libffi. There is a compatible version of libffi
    in python3 sources (Modules/_ctypes/libffi) but the libffi
    package installed on the system can be used if --with-system-ffi
    configure flag is used (this is how the Yocto recipe from upstream
    works starting with 3.5.6 version).
    
    For the hardknott default version of python3 (3.9.5) the libffi
    from the sysroot is compatible (v3.3) and the _ctypes module
    is compiled. But for the 3.6.12 version, the configure configure
    for _ctypes modules fails because of incompatible libffi:
    
    warning: building with the bundled copy of libffi is deprecated
    on this platform.  It will not be distributed with Python 3.7
    env: tmp/work/snr-64-intelaxxia-linux/python3/3.6.12-r0/Python-3.6.12/\
         Modules/_ctypes/libffi/configure: No such file or directory
    Failed to configure _ctypes module
    
    The build doesn't fail, but on target the _ctypes module is not found:
    
    root@intel-axxia-snr:~# python
    Python 3.6.12 (default, Aug 15 2020, 06:59:32)
    [GCC 11.2.0] on linux
    Type "help", "copyright", "credits" or "license" for more information.
    >>> import _ctypes
    Traceback (most recent call last):
      File "<stdin>", line 1, in <module>
    ModuleNotFoundError: No module named '_ctypes'
    
    To fix this, we need to run autoreconf in Modules/_ctypes/libffi in
    order to use the in-tree version of libffi for python3.6.
    
    A0344 - GRR/SNR -- Add Python3 Ctypes
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>

