commit 49b3e018155645344f730f102a6545e109143163
Author: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 11 16:32:40 2021 +0300

    elfutils: Fix libdir path for multilib SDK
    
    In a multilib SDK environment, compiling tools/objtools from a
    kernel tree fails because the linker cannot find libc libraries:
    /usr/bin/ld: cannot find /lib64/libc.so.6
    /usr/bin/ld: cannot find /usr/lib64/libc_nonshared.a
    
    In a kernel tree, LDFLAGS variable from tools/objtools/Makefile
    contains LIBELF_LIBS variable which gets the libdir flags for libelf
    using pkg-config:
    LIBELF_LIBS := $(shell pkg-config libelf --libs 2>/dev/null)
    
    pkg-config will look into <SDK>/usr/lib64/pkgconfig/libelf.pc in
    order to find libdir path which in a multilib SDK is /usr/lib64.
    
    When looking for libraries in <SDK>/usr/lib64 the libc.so library
    is an ASCII test file pointing to a host location:
    
    [ddragomi]$ file libc.so
    libc.so: ASCII text
    
    [ddragomi]$ cat libc.so
    /* GNU ld script
       Use the shared library, but some functions are only in
       the static library, so try that secondarily.  */
    OUTPUT_FORMAT(elf64-x86-64)
    GROUP ( /lib64/libc.so.6 /usr/lib64/libc_nonshared.a
            AS_NEEDED ( /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 ) )
    
    Here we have a host contamination which behaves different depending
    on the Linux distribution where the SDK is run:
    - Fedora and Slackware has 64-bit libraries in /lib64 and 32-bit
      libraries in /lib and the build works
    - Ubuntu has 64-bit libraries in /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu and 32-bit
      libraries in /lib/i386-linux-gnu and the build fails with the
      missing libraries message.
    
    To avoid this host contamination, we can replace libdir (/usr/lib64
    for multilib) path to point to base_libdir (/lib64 for multilib) in
    libelf.pc to force LDFLAGS to point to <SDK>/lib64 path where the SDK
    have good libc libraries.
    
    When cross-compiling using yocto SDK we should use SDK binaries and
    libraries as much as we can and avoid those from host.
    
    B0242 - GRR/SNR -- Multilib 'external-modules-setup.sh' Fails
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>

