Author: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>
Date:   Tue Apr 27 01:21:14 2021 +0300

    python3-docutils: Native class extension breaks libvirt
    
    In hardknott branch, there are 2 versions of python3-docutils module:
    0.17 in meta-openembedded/meta-python and 0.16 in poky.
    
    Only the 0.16 version from poky extends bbclass to native in order to
    build packages which depends on python3-docutils-native such as libvirt.
    
    With this unversioned bbappend recipe we extend bbclass to native for
    0.17 version too. And by default, bitbake uses the latest version when
    multiple versions are availabe. But libvirt 6.3.0 fails to build with
    python3-docutils 0.17 with the following parsing errors (e.g.):
    | kbase/qemu-passthrough-security.html.in:299: namespace error :
            Failed to parse QName 'http:'
    |   /* optimum is 45…75 characters/line <http://webtypography.net/2.1.2> */
    
    Remove native bbclass extension from generic bbappend recipe in order
    to build and use python3-docutils 0.16 version for native requests
    (such as libvirt 6.3.0 build). But keep nativesdk bbclass extension
    since nativesdk-python3-docutils is a runtime dependency for
    nativesdk-python3-robotframework which is included in Axxia SDK.
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>

