Author: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>
Date:   Thu Feb 25 18:11:01 2021 +0000

    initscripts-readonly-rootfs-overlay: Remove 'mode=' default mount option
    
    ROOT_RWMOUNTOPTIONS_DEVICE variable from init-readonly-rootfs-overlay-boot.sh
    script defaults to "rw,noatime,mode=755" and represent the mount options of
    the read-write file system (upperdir for the overlayfs). Those mount options
    are used when a real device/partition is set in ROOT_RWDEVICE variable via
    'rootrw' kernel command line parameter.
    
    Virtual filesystems such as tmpfs, devpts and non-Unix filesystems such as
    vfat, ntfs, generally filesystems that do not have their own file rights
    (in the Unix sense), typically have the ability to set permissions using
    the mount option. But extN are native Unix filesystem, so the rights in
    it are used and 'mode=value' mount option is not supported:
    
    EXT4-fs (sda1): Unrecognized mount option "mode=755" or missing value
    
    So, remove 'mode=755' as default mount options for the he read-write
    file system. Those mount options can also be overwritten also via
    rootrwoptions Kernel command line parameter as described in README.
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>

