    busybox-udhcpc: Handle case when rootfs is mounted as overlayfs
    
    The custom axxia rc.local script run on the end of the boot
    process the udhcpc command for the main network interface eth0
    in order to populate resolv.conf with nameservers from dhcp lease.
    The dpcp client calls the /etc/udhcpc.d/50default script which
    check first (in root_is_nfs function) if the interface is used for
    nfsroot and skip ip commands which can break nfs conectivity.
    
    This patch is handling the case when the rootfs is mounted as
    overlayfs by overwriting the root_is_nfs function: extracts the
    lowerdir directory of the overlay (the read-only rootfs) and check
    if this is mounted via nfs|smbfs|ncp|coda and takes actions to not
    break conectivity.
    
    Otherwise the board will freeze on the end of the boot and after
    timeout will reboot.
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>

commit 540fbcf8212f7a1b9bdb1ef5077fc3efb05bc679
