    The main purpose for nfsroot script is to check if one interface is
    used for nfsroot and to skip ifup fot it, in order to not lose nfs
    response. In this case, resolv.conf is not populating the file with
    nameservers from dhcp lease. This script fixes this by creating a
    symlink /etc/resolv.conf to /proc/net/pnp as recomanded in the
    official kernel documentation.
    
    This patch is handling the case when the rootfs is mounted as overlayfs:
    it extracts the lowerdir directory of the overlay (the read-only rootfs)
    and check if this is mounted via nfs and takes actions. It also extracts
    the nfs_addr from lowerdir mount options instead from the root mount.
    
