commit 2d372cbda1afefdd5a8f0f95f8496e8c2917f079
Author: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>
Date:   Fri Jan 8 21:12:32 2021 +0000

    Fix resolv.conf symlink for read-only rootfs
    
    If one network interface is used for nfsroot, we overwrite the
    actual /etc/resolv.conf symlink to points to /proc/net/pnp as
    recommended in the the kernel official documentation. But this
    fails in a read-only rootfs:
    
    ln: failed to create symbolic link '/etc/resolv.conf': Read-only file system
    
    By default, in a sysvinit based system, /etc/resolv.conf points
    to /var/run/resolv.conf which is located in a tmpfs partition.
    
    To cover the read-only case, we'll overwrite the volatile symlink
    from /var/run each time when an interface is used for nfsroot:
    
    /etc/resolv.conf(ro) -> /var/run/resolv.conf(rw) -> /proc/net/pnp(ro)
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>

