Author: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>
Date:   Thu Jul 16 10:46:34 2020 +0000

    rdk-tools: Fix SHM and RPC modes with LTTng enabled
    
    When LTTng support is enabled for SHM mode, rdk userspace
    require lttng-ust (contains the userspace tracer library
    to trace userspace codes) as build dependency in order to
    find in sysroot tracepoint.h header and liblttng-ust.so
    library:
    
    | checking for LTTng with pkg-config... no
    | checking lttng/tracepoint.h usability... no
    | checking lttng/tracepoint.h presence... no
    | checking for lttng/tracepoint.h... no
    | configure: error: LTTng requires header tracepoint.h
    
    Also, when LTTng support is enabled for RPC mode, rdk userspace
    require also lttng-tools to be installed in recipe sysroot and
    LTTNG_ROOT variable should point to sysroot path where its headers
    are installed (include/lttng/lttng.h). This is the nanual check for
    lttng support (without pkg-config which uses some host paths and
    causes QA errors regarding include location unsafe for
    cross-compilation):
    
    | checking for LTTng with pkg-config... no
    | configure: error: RPC requires --with-lttng if LTTng enabled.
    
    With this patch the compile log with LTTng support enabled looks like:
    
    checking for LTTng in <$LTTNG_ROOT> ... yes
    checking lttng/tracepoint.h usability... yes
    checking lttng/tracepoint.h presence... yes
    checking for lttng/tracepoint.h... yes
    checking for library containing lttng_ust_init... -llttng-ust
    configure: LOGGING: lttng
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>

