Author: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>
Date:   Mon Mar 23 12:17:53 2020 +0000

    coreutils: Fix conflicts in multilib build
    
    The new ptest dependencies present some challenges, in particular
    libmodule-build-perl which effectively depends on gcc. In multilib
    images, this results in both libXX-gcc-symlinks and libYY-gcc-symlinks
    being installed which conflict.
    
    Move libmodule-build-perl from RDEPENDS to RRECOMMENDS in order to get
    rid of the following errors on image do_rootfs. If in RDEPENDS bitbake
    will try to install libmodule-build-perl and if lib32-gcc have conflicts
    with gcc it will exit with error. If in RRECOMENDS bitbake will not exit
    with error if it's unable to install libmodule-build-perl and his gcc and
    lib32-gcc dependencies.
    
    Error: Transaction check error:
      file /usr/bin/gcc conflicts between attempted installs of gcc-symlinks-9.3.0-r0.core2_64 and lib32-gcc-symlinks-9.3.0-r0.core2_32
      file /usr/bin/cpp conflicts between attempted installs of cpp-symlinks-9.3.0-r0.core2_64 and lib32-cpp-symlinks-9.3.0-r0.core2_32
      file /usr/bin/g++ conflicts between attempted installs of lib32-g++-symlinks-9.3.0-r0.core2_32 and g++-symlinks-9.3.0-r0.core2_64
    
    Related:
    http://lists.openembedded.org/pipermail/openembedded-core/2020-March/294143.html
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>

