Author: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 18 17:12:59 2019 +0000

    meta-environment: Set HOST_EXTRACFLAGS in SDK environment
    
    If the SDK is used to compile external kernels, there were some host
    programs inside kernel tree which are using HOSTCC (gcc) compiler
    instead CC (CROSS_COMPILE-gcc). Host programs are defined in kernel
    Makefiles utilizing the variable hostprogs-y (more details here:
    https://www.kernel.org/doc/Documentation/kbuild/makefiles.txt).
    
    When compiling host programs, it is possible to set specific flags.
    The programs will always be compiled utilizing $(HOSTCC) passed
    the options specified in $(KBUILD_HOSTCFLAGS).
    To set flags that will take effect for all host programs created
    in that Makefile, we need to use the variable HOST_EXTRACFLAGS.
    
    Since HOSTCC is the gcc compiler from the host, it will search for
    headers, linkers or other dependencies on the host rootfs. Using
    HOST_EXTRACFLAGS we can tell kbuild to search for headers (-I flag)
    or linkers (-L flag) in OECORE_NATIVE_SYSROOT patch which is the
    host part of the SDK: x86_64-intelaxxiasdk-linux directory.
    
    So, export HOST_EXTRACFLAGS from SDK environment-setup scripts:
    HOST_EXTRACFLAGS="-I$OECORE_NATIVE_SYSROOT/usr/include \
                      -L$OECORE_NATIVE_SYSROOT/usr/lib"
    
    B0169 - Fail to build x86 standalone kernel 4.19 using SDK
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>

