    Fix multilib install binaries conflicts
    
    In a multilib build, some update-alternatives warnings are showing
    that multiple providers for some binaries were installed with
    the same priority:
    
    [log_check] axxia-image-vcn: found 6 warning messages in the logfile:
    [log_check] Warn: update-alternatives: libtool has multiple providers with
        the same priority, please check /usr/lib/opkg/alternatives/libtool
    [log_check] Warn: update-alternatives: icu-config has multiple providers
        with the same priority, please check usr/lib/opkg/alternatives/icu-config
    [log_check] Warn: update-alternatives: g-ir-annotation-tool has multiple
        providers with the same priority, please check
        /usr/lib/opkg/alternatives/g-ir-annotation-tool
    [log_check] Warn: update-alternatives: g-ir-scanner has multiple providers
        with the same priority, please check /usr/lib/opkg/alternatives/g-ir-scanner
    [log_check] Warn: update-alternatives: python-config has multiple providers with
        the same priority, please check /usr/lib/opkg/alternatives/python-config
    [log_check] Warn: update-alternatives: gpgrt-config has multiple providers with
        the same priority, please check /usr/lib/opkg/alternatives/gpgrt-config
    
    The update-alternatives class is used to register a binary provided
    by a package that may have an alternative implementation in a some
    other package. But the case when the alternative binary cames from
    the multilib version of the package is handled by multilib_script
    class which mark up those binaries so that they can be handled
    using update-alternatives.
    
    For icu-config binary, we have in /usr/lib/opkg/alternatives/icu-config:
    /usr/bin/icu-config
    /usr/bin/icu-config-lib64 10
    /usr/bin/icu-config-lib 10
    
    We set lower priority for multilib package (lib32-*) which provides
    /usr/bin/icu-config-lib and highter for the default version
    /usr/bin/icu-config-lib64 through ALTERNATIVE_PRIORITY variable.
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>

