    linux: Add support for multiple kernel versions
    
    Implement the ability to build multiple kernels in one build.
    Alternative kernels will be installed in deploy directory under
    separate kernel-<PN> folder and also in rootfs on /boot
    directory. Kernels can be swhitch by recreating the bzImage
    symlink. Default is the kernel set as preferred provider for
    virtual/kernel.
    
    Note that all the kernel modules archives should be deployed
    for each kernel version as we do for virtual/kernel provider.
    Archives with kernel modules are found in each separate
    kernel-<PN> folder from deploy dir.
    
    More details about multiple kernels support:
    http://lists.openembedded.org/pipermail/openembedded-core/2017-October/143535.html
    
    If don't want to build alternative kernels, just reset
    ALTERNATIVE_KERNELS variable in local.conf:
    ALTERNATIVE_KERNELS = ""
    
    A0283 - Multiple Linux Kernels in the Same Yocto Build
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <Daniel.Dragomir@windriver.com>

