    dhclient: Fix resolv.conf if interface is used for nfsroot
    
    If the main interface is used for nfsroot, dhclient skip it
    by calling dhclient-systemd-wrapper. In this case, resolv.conf
    continue to be maintained by systemd-resolvd service which is
    not populating the file with nameservers from dhcp lease.
    
    In the kernel official documentation [1], it is recomanded to
    symlink /etc/resolv.conf to /proc/net/pnp on systems that use
    an NFS root filesystem.
    
    So, we append dhclient-systemd-wrapper to create that symlink
    if nfsroot flag is different than default value (0).
    
    [1] https://www.kernel.org/doc/Documentation/filesystems/nfs/nfsroot.txt
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <daniel.dragomir@windriver.com>

