Date:   Thu Apr 11 13:22:57 2019 +0300

    conf/distro: Disable building introspection data using qemu
    
    Starting with commit 761fd4343378 ("axxiax86-64: Create tuning
    file with sse4.2 support") axxiax86_64 machine is built using a
    custom tuning file with sse4.2 support which is unknown for gcc
    and unsuported for quemu. We have disable qemu-usermode feature
    for the machine, but as a consequence, 'update_gio_module_cache
    'and 'update_font_cache' postinstall intercept hooks could not
    be executed and raises warnings.
    
    To avoid those warnings, we need to disable those postinstall
    intercept hooks by reseting GIO_MODULE_PACKAGES and FONT_PACKAGES
    variables. Because it's not ok to reset this in the machine
    configuration file, we did it in the distro file.
    
    Also, since meta-intel-snr layer will be used in some cases
    separate of meta-intel-axxia, we disable building introspection
    data using qemu through BACKFILL_CONSIDERED mechanism for
    'gobject-introspection-data' distro features even if the same
    effect has the 'qemu-usermode' machine feature which is also
    added to BACKFILL_CONSIDERED in the machine configuration file.
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <daniel.dragomir@windriver.com>

