Author: Daniel Dragomir <daniel.dragomir@windriver.com>
Date:   Fri Feb 15 16:43:54 2019 +0200

    linux: Enable kvm support for all kernel versions
    
    KVM kernel options are now enabled only for 4.19 kernel, but
    kernel-module-kvm* sub-packages are included in axxia-image-vcn
    unconditionally. If a different kernel version is built, KVM
    options will not be enabled in kernel config, and there will be
    no kvm modules built and no kernel-module-kvm sub-package created.
    The build will fail on do_rootfs with:
    
    ERROR: axxia-image-vcn-1.0-r0 do_rootfs: Could not invoke dnf.
    No match for argument: kernel-module-kvm-amd
    No match for argument: kernel-module-kvm
    No match for argument: kernel-module-kvm-intel
    Error: Unable to find a match
    
    The right way to have KVM support is to add kvm distro feature
    from meta-virtualization layer in our disto. This feature will
    all the kernel options and some other settings for KVM.
    
    In order to enable KVM support for all our kernel versions,
    we'll require linux-yocto_virtualization.inc in linux-axxia.inc
    because meta-virtualization enables KVM support only for official
    supported kernel versions: linux-yocto 4.14 and 4.18.
    
    And to get rid of all the warnings for duplicating inclusion of
    linux-yocto_virtualization.inc, we'll skip parsing linux-yocto
    bbappend recipes from meta-virtualization through BBMASK mechanism.
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <daniel.dragomir@windriver.com>

