commit 073eadf917237d3e2286473bebd3fbbbff0ab93f
Author: Daniel Dragomir <daniel.dragomir@windriver.com>
Date:   Thu Jan 3 17:22:24 2019 +0200

    kernel-devsrc: Add missing files for Makefile "clean" target
    
    Starting with commit 9af0f1a46bbb6ad9ee8b35957251f4aa826b023f
    ("kernel-devsrc: restructure for out of tree (and on target) module
    builds") from poky repo, the way how kernel-devsrc package is
    created was changed.
    
    The old kernel-devsrc package starts with a full copy of the kernel
    source and then starts to strip out elements that are not required.
    
    This restructuring of the package uses an approach similar to other
    distros, where the kernel-devsrc package is for building against the
    running kernel and uses a curated set of copied infrastructure, versus
    a mass copy of the entire kernel.
    
    More details about this change here:
    https://patches.openembedded.org/patch/152442
    
    This patch add in kernel-devsrc some Makefiles, Kbuild and .mk files
    required to perform the "clean" target.
    
    A0261 - After Installing the SDK, 'make clean oldconfig scripts
            tools/objtool' Fails
    
    Signed-off-by: Daniel Dragomir <daniel.dragomir@windriver.com>

