    Update the File System Image Names
    
    Instead of axxia-image-large and axxia-image-large-sdk, add
    axxia-image-vcn.  This is axxia-image-large-sdk.  In practice,
    axxia-image-large is not used.
    
    axxia-image-small is meant for use as a small ramdisk (initial
    ramdisk during boot, for example).
    
    axxia-image-sim is meant for use in simulation, although it will
    work on hardware.  It should provide the functionality needed to
    run the RDK samples, but not much more.
    
    axxia-image-vcn is meant for use as a disk/usb image, or nfs mounted
    root file system.  It includes the SDK and LTP, as well as many more
    useful utilities.  It can be used in simulation, but is much larger
    than axxia-image-sim.
    
    Signed-off-by: John Jacques <john.jacques@intel.com>

